      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Aggregate vs per-request throughput",
      "description": "The single most important chart for a token-billing service. Decoding is memory-bandwidth bound: one token requires reading every weight. Serving N requests from one weight read is what makes tokens cheap. AGGREGATE tokens/sec should climb with concurrency while PER-REQUEST speed falls \u2014 that divergence is your margin being created. Where the aggregate line flattens is your batch ceiling.",
